{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "EZK",
  "chapter": 24,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "EZK.24.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.24.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Again in the ninth year, in the tenth month, in the tenth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "day",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of the month, the word of the LORD came to me, saying,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.24.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.24.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Son of man, Write for thee the name of the day, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of this same day: the king of Babylon set himself against Jerusalem this same day.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.24.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.24.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And utter a parable to the rebellious house, and say to them, Thus saith the Lord GOD; Set on a pot, set ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " on, and also pour water into it:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.24.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.24.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Gather its pieces into it, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " every good piece, the thigh, and the shoulder; fill ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with the choice bones.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.24.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.24.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Take the choice of the flock, and burn also the bones under it, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " make it boil well, and let them boil its bones in it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.24.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.24.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Wherefore thus saith the Lord GOD; Woe to the bloody city, to the pot whose scum ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " therein, and whose scum is not gone out of it! bring it out piece by piece; let no lot fall upon it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.24.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.24.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For her blood is in the midst of her; she set it upon the top of a rock; she poured it not upon the ground, to cover it with dust;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.24.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.24.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That it might cause fury to come up to take vengeance; I have set her blood upon the top of a rock, that it should not be covered.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.24.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.24.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD; Woe to the bloody city! I will even make the pile for fire great.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.24.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.24.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Heap on wood, kindle the fire, consume the flesh, and spice it well, and let the bones be burned.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.24.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.24.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then set it empty upon its coals, that the brass of it may be hot, and may burn, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the filthiness of it may be melted in it, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the scum of it may be consumed.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.24.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.24.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "She hath wearied ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "herself",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with lies, and her great scum went not forth out of her: her scum ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shall be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in the fire.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.24.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.24.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "In thy filthiness ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " lewdness: because I have purged thee, and thou wast not purged, thou shalt not be purged from thy filthiness any more, till I have caused my fury to rest upon thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.24.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.24.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I the LORD have spoken ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": "; it shall come to pass, and I will do ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": "; I will not go back, neither will I spare, neither will I repent; according to thy ways, and according to thy doings, shall they judge thee, saith the Lord GOD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.24.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.24.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Also the word of the LORD came to me, saying,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.24.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.24.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Son of man, behold, I take away from thee the desire of thy eyes with a stroke: yet neither shalt thou mourn nor weep, neither shall thy tears run down.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.24.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.24.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Forbear to cry, make no mourning for the dead, bind the tire of thy head upon thee, and put on thy shoes upon thy feet, and cover not ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "thy",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " lips, and eat not the bread of men.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.24.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.24.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So I spoke to the people in the morning: and at evening my wife died; and I did in the morning as I was commanded.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.24.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.24.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the people said to me, Wilt thou not tell us what these ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "things are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to us, that thou doest ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "so",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": "?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.24.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.24.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then I answered them, the word of the LORD came to me, saying,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.24.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.24.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Speak to the house of Israel, Thus saith the Lord GOD; Behold, I will profane my sanctuary, the excellence of your strength, the desire of your eyes, and that which your soul pitieth; and your sons and your daughters whom ye have left shall fall by the sword.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.24.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.24.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And ye shall do as I have done: ye shall not cover ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "your",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " lips, nor eat the bread of men.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.24.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.24.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And your tires ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shall be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " upon your heads, and your shoes upon your feet: ye shall not mourn nor weep; but ye shall pine away for your iniquities, and mourn one towards another.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.24.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.24.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thus Ezekiel is to you a sign: according to all that he hath done shall ye do: and when this cometh, ye shall know that I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the Lord GOD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.24.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.24.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Also, thou son of man, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shall it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in the day when I take from them their strength, the joy of their glory, the desire of their eyes, and that on which they set their minds, their sons and their daughters,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.24.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.24.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he that escapeth in that day shall come to thee, to cause ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "thee",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to hear ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "thy",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " ears?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.24.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.24.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "In that day shall thy mouth be opened to him who hath escaped, and thou shalt speak, and be no more dumb: and thou shalt be a sign to them; and they shall know that I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
